---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = false;
Astro.cache.set({ maxAge: 86400, swr: 604800 });
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions — Live AQI"
  description="The terms for using Live AQI: an information service for real-time air quality, not medical advice. Data sources, alerts, acceptable use and liability."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <section class="stage">
    <div class="shell pt-10 pb-12 lg:pt-14 lg:pb-16">
      <h1 class="type-hero max-w-4xl">Terms &amp; conditions</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-on-stage-muted">
        The short version: Live AQI is free information about the air, offered in good faith. Use it to make better
        decisions, not as a medical or emergency service.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="shell py-12 lg:py-16">
    <div class="prose-reading">
      <p class="text-sm text-subtle">Last updated 19 November 2026</p>

      <h2>Using Live AQI</h2>
      <p>
        These terms apply to live-aqi.com and its notifications (together, “Live AQI”). By using Live AQI you agree to them.
        If you don’t agree, please don’t use the site. Live AQI is free and works without an account.
      </p>

      <h2>Information, not medical advice</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Live AQI shows air quality readings, forecasts and general health guidance based on official index statements. It is not medical advice and does not replace advice from a doctor.</li>
        <li>Live AQI does not issue official advisories or emergency warnings. In an emergency, or when your local health or environment authority gives instructions, follow them.</li>
        <li>If you have a health condition that air pollution affects, talk to a healthcare professional about what levels are safe for you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>About the data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Readings are computed from model data (the Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service, delivered by Open-Meteo) and, where enabled, ground monitoring stations. Model values can differ from a nearby monitor, and forecasts are uncertain by nature.</li>
        <li>Each reading is labelled with its time and source. When a provider is unavailable, Live AQI shows an error or the last real data with its age; it never invents values.</li>
        <li>All data is provided “as is”, without any promise that it is complete, accurate or available at all times. How Live AQI calculates each index is explained in the <a href="/methodology">methodology</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Alerts and notifications</h2>
      <p>
        Alerts are a convenience. In-page alerts only run while a Live AQI page is open, and background notifications depend
        on your browser, your device settings and your browser’s push service. Notifications can be delayed or not arrive at
        all, so don’t rely on them as your only warning of dangerous air. You can turn them off at any time on the{' '}
        <a href="/alerts">alerts page</a> or in your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use Live AQI for personal, non-commercial information, or link to its pages freely.</li>
        <li>Don’t scrape the site or call its <code>/api/</code> endpoints in bulk or from automated systems; requests are rate-limited to protect the shared data quotas that keep Live AQI free.</li>
        <li>Don’t attempt to disrupt, overload or gain unauthorised access to the service, or present Live AQI data as an official government reading.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data sources and attribution</h2>
      <p>
        Live AQI is built on open data, each under its own licence: air quality and weather from{' '}
        <a href="https://open-meteo.com/" rel="noopener">Open-Meteo</a> (CC BY 4.0) using the{' '}
        <a href="https://atmosphere.copernicus.eu/" rel="noopener">Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service</a>; places from{' '}
        <a href="https://www.geonames.org/" rel="noopener">GeoNames</a> (CC BY 4.0) and{' '}
        <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap</a> (ODbL); map tiles from{' '}
        <a href="https://openfreemap.org/" rel="noopener">OpenFreeMap</a>. If you reuse any of that data, the original
        provider’s licence applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Our content</h2>
      <p>
        The Live AQI name, logo, design, illustrations, text and software are owned by Live AQI and may not be copied or
        reused without permission, apart from sharing links and screenshots with attribution.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        Live AQI links to data providers and other websites. We are not responsible for their content, availability or
        privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Live AQI is provided without warranties of any kind, and Live AQI is not
        liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of the site, its data or its notifications, or from decisions
        made using them. Nothing in these terms limits any rights you have that cannot be limited by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may change or discontinue features, and update these terms when the service changes. The date at the top shows the
        latest version; continuing to use Live AQI after a change means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:contact@live-aqi.com">contact@live-aqi.com</a>, or see the{' '}
        <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. How we handle personal data is covered in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
